{
  "_comment": "Layer-gate targets of security-slow.sh `mutate` (slither-mutate), `gambit` (Gambit) and `necessist`. Each entry names a src/ folder (not its subfolders); every implementation file in it (a contract or a library with functions) is mutated, and its mutants are run against the Foundry tests matched by `tests` (a forge --match-path glob). `files` (optional) limits an entry to the implementation files whose name matches one of its globs, so one folder can map different files to different tests; the contracts at the top of src/ and the shared src/libraries/ and src/integrations/ folders list theirs. Necessist removes statements from the same test files. A folder without an implementation file has no mutants. `gambit` sets the seed, operators and per-file mutant cap of each layer for security-gambit.sh (`script/mutation-targets.py gambit`).",
